    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it passes. The full `mvn test` build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `customerCode` assignment so that `POST /api/owners` assigns a code formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` and it's returned via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter.\n\n2. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `customerCode` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `displayName`/`initials`), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it and MapStruct maps it by name.\n\n3. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 in `addOwner`, after defaulting the registration date, assign `owner.setCustomerCode(nextCustomerCode(owner.getLastName()))` before saving. The new `nextCustomerCode` helper builds `LAST3` from the upper-cased first three letters of `lastName` and `NNNN` as `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, zero-padded to 4 digits (`String.format(\"%s-%04d\", ...)`).\n\n4. **`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`** \u2014 added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table (tests run on the hsqldb profile; the others updated for consistency).\n\nBecause each create counts existing owners then saves, two sequential creates (`smithers` then `jones`) produce e.g. `SMI-000N` and `JON-000(N+1)` \u2014 satisfying the test's `startsWith` and `+1` sequence assertions. `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` passes and the overall build is green.",
